NAME
  qboot - build and control the QuickOS compressed boot archive

SYNOPSIS
  qboot build [options]
  qboot enable [options]
  qboot status [--json]
  qboot restore [--json]
  qboot disable [--json]

DESCRIPTION
  build creates an inactive QBoot image from the current QuickOS boot files.
  enable activates an existing build, or builds one first when none exists.
  restore and disable restore the preserved normal init.lua while retaining the build.
  status reports whether QBoot is built and enabled.

OPTIONS
  --archive-layout=per-file|solid
    Compress files independently (default) or as one stream.

  --archive-storage=sidecar|embedded
    Store compressed bytes in /.qboot/archive.lzss (default) or init.lua.

  --no-boot-screen
    Suppress the initial QuickOS boot logo drawing.

  --diagnostics
    Include decompression diagnostics. This slows boot and is not intended for normal use.

  --json
    Print command results as JSON.
